A||||1||Philphine||pretty good fiero day  (long)||||1||
Z||000000||Philphine||05-18-2001||08:40 PM||||running an errand this morning close to home but not in a direction i usually go in and saw a pretty nice fiero at a garage. stopped to ask who it belonded to and it was one of the mechanics. gave him the forum addy. told him i had a couple and he asked if i lived where he had seen a couple. it was me. hope he shows up here. seemed to like his fiero.<P>then on the way to work i saw another i hadn'd seen in a few years in one of our other company lots. i hadn't seen it since i joined the forum and don't really know the guy anyway (office big wig i think). really nice gt with mecham scoops. left a note on his car with the web addy and mentioned i was in the building across the street.<P>also making progress on the chin spoiler. i've decided not to try to graft them together but i did cut out the facia to make one big opening. done some filling in and bracing today. not done yet, but it looks like it's going to be doable and look pretty good.<P>and last, i should get my first v6 in a few months. i was in a pawn shop earlier this week (another reason why i'm always broke) and as i was leaving i saw a gt behind the fence. never noticed it before even though i'm by there all the time. went back in and found out they've had it for a long time but a truck was in front of it facing the road. an '86 1/2 4 speed gt, silver. went back today. they believe it's sat so long the fuels gummed up (said it was running when pawned, back in '99). they had a mechanic look at it and said it needs a new fuel pump. appearance wise it looks good. engine dosen't look too dirty (kinda good indication) power every thing but no cruise.hooked up a battery to try the power assesories, they work. seat covers over kind of ragged seats. it's a pawn shop so i put it on layaway. no interest but i have to pay it off before i can get it. $1200. kind of a gamble since i can't check it better but it seems worth the risk.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe (cheap thrill)<BR>'84 chop top (parts car or project. time will tell)<p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 05-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||05-18-2001||11:21 PM||||I rarely see other Fieros parked and in good enough condition to where I can leave a note, but I do see some pretty well kept ones drive by at the store where I work.  I have seen 2 Fieros actually come in and park, and I have waited on both of those people and talked a little about thier cars with them.  One guy was really interested, the other one, well, he said he was restoring it, but he just wasnt very friendly at all.<P>who knows, but for the most part, everyone that I have met that has a Fiero, has loved them and keeps them looking and running good.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
